strings.MEX_DoctorsStrike_info_tooltip:
To address the ongoing illegal labor actions occurring in hospitals throughout the country, we must collaborate with the IMSS, the ISSTE, CNOP, and, of course, our security services. While these bodies suggest many approaches to deal with the strikers, all agree that a bloody and costly crackdown would be forced upon us if we failed to keep the strikes' Radicalism in check.
Additional information can be found in the Crisis report, but the consensus is that Radicalism must be equal to or below the following targets for this stage of the strikes:
£GFX_DoctorsStrike_interns Intern £GFX_PRI_GUI_ds_target_radicalism Target Radicalism: {intern_target_radicalism}
£GFX_DoctorsStrike_doctors Doctor £GFX_PRI_GUI_ds_target_radicalism Target Radicalism: {doctor_target_radicalism}

strings.MEX_PRI_kabuki_pact_strength_ttd:
{root_pact_strength_effect_giver}

£GFX_MEX_PRI_crisis_pact_strength Pact-Strength above 80 will ensure Madrazo's supremacy in the pact, whereas a £GFX_MEX_PRI_crisis_pact_strength Pact-Strength below 20 will weaken the pact, leaving Ordaz the stronger individual.

As long as either Ordaz or Madrazo sway the £mex_industrialists_texticon The Industrialists, £mex_party_officials_texticon The Party Bureaucracy, and £mex_workers_texticon The Workers, their plans will continue unaltered. However, they must sway £mex_dfs_texticon The DFS to their individual side for their final victory.
